# webroot-drift.ignore
#
# One pattern per line, rsync --exclude syntax. Comments (#) and blank lines
# are ignored. Patterns added here are layered on top of the defaults baked
# into scripts/webroot-drift-detector.sh.
#
# Use this file for site-specific runtime/noise files that legitimately exist
# in the webroot but should not be considered drift.

# Example: ad-hoc client report drops served from the webroot
# client-reports/

# Example: pa11y output left behind after a deploy verify
# pa11y-output.txt
